{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "---\n",
        "title: \"Quick EDA on Simulation Output\"\n",
        "format: html\n",
        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "## What This Code Does\n",
        "\n",
        "This demo reads the CSV tables produced by a simulation run — `model.csv` and `agent.csv` — and produces a quick exploratory data analysis. It shows data shapes, summary statistics, agent-level aggregates, and step-level trends.\n",
        "\n",
        "The code uses `pandas` `.info()` and `.describe()` for data shape and distribution, then groups by `AgentID` and `Step` to compute mean PSS-10, resilience, and current stress.\n",
        "\n",
        "## Setup"
      ],
      "id": "f04f1d33"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#| label: setup\n",
        "import os\n",
        "import sys\n",
        "import pathlib\n",
        "import numpy as np\n",
        "import pandas as pd\n",
        "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
        "\n",
        "demos_dir = pathlib.Path(os.getcwd())\n",
        "project_root = demos_dir.parents[2]\n",
        "sys.path.insert(0, str(project_root))\n",
        "\n",
        "DATA_PATH = project_root / \"data\" / \"raw\""
      ],
      "id": "setup",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Loading Data\n",
        "\n",
        "We read the two output tables into DataFrames and inspect their structure."
      ],
      "id": "88122445"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#| label: load\n",
        "try:\n",
        "    tbl_model = pd.read_csv(DATA_PATH / \"model.csv\")\n",
        "    tbl_agent = pd.read_csv(DATA_PATH / \"agent.csv\")\n",
        "    HAS_DATA = True\n",
        "    print(\"=== MODEL TABLE ===\")\n",
        "    tbl_model.info()\n",
        "    print(\"\\n=== AGENT TABLE ===\")\n",
        "    tbl_agent.info()\n",
        "except FileNotFoundError:\n",
        "    print(\"Simulation data not found. Run a simulation first to produce model.csv and agent.csv.\")\n",
        "    HAS_DATA = False"
      ],
      "id": "load",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Summary Statistics"
      ],
      "id": "d942b167"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#| label: describe\n",
        "if HAS_DATA:\n",
        "    print(\"=== MODEL SUMMARY ===\")\n",
        "    display(tbl_model.describe().T)\n",
        "    print(\"\\n=== AGENT SUMMARY ===\")\n",
        "    display(tbl_agent.describe().T)"
      ],
      "id": "describe",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Grouped Aggregates"
      ],
      "id": "b94f3993"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#| label: groupby\n",
        "if HAS_DATA:\n",
        "    agent_summary = (\n",
        "        tbl_agent.groupby(\"AgentID\")\n",
        "        .agg({\"pss10\": \"mean\", \"resilience\": \"mean\", \"current_stress\": \"mean\"})\n",
        "        .rename(columns={\"pss10\": \"avg_pss10\", \"resilience\": \"avg_resilience\", \"current_stress\": \"avg_stress\"})\n",
        "    )\n",
        "    print(\"=== AGENT-LEVEL AVERAGES ===\")\n",
        "    display(agent_summary)\n",
        "\n",
        "    step_summary = (\n",
        "        tbl_agent.groupby(\"Step\")\n",
        "        .agg({\"pss10\": \"mean\", \"resilience\": \"mean\", \"current_stress\": \"mean\"})\n",
        "        .rename(columns={\"pss10\": \"avg_pss10\", \"resilience\": \"avg_resilience\", \"current_stress\": \"avg_stress\"})\n",
        "    )\n",
        "    print(\"\\n=== STEP-LEVEL AVERAGES ===\")\n",
        "    display(step_summary)"
      ],
      "id": "groupby",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Why This Matters for the Simulation\n",
        "\n",
        "Quick EDA is the first step in validating simulation runs. By checking agent-level and step-level aggregates, we can spot convergence issues, outlier agents, or unexpected drift in key variables before running formal analyses.\n",
        "\n",
        "## What We See\n",
        "\n",
        "- Data shape tells us how many agents and time steps were recorded\n",
        "- Summary statistics reveal range, mean, and variance of core variables\n",
        "- Agent-level aggregates highlight individual differences in stress and resilience\n",
        "- Step-level aggregates show population-wide trends over the simulation timeline"
      ],
      "id": "1bd232a7"
    }
  ],
